# The dirty-page artifact, not fixture data.
#
# `rebuildIndex` and the multi-item write path both drop one of these into the
# content directory, so `copyFixtures` sweeps it into whatever fixture was
# being generated. It carries a wall-clock `updatedAt`, so committing it means
# a spurious diff every time a fixture is regenerated — and nothing in this
# suite reads it. A real content repository ignores it for the same reason
# (`initializeContentGit`); the demo's fixtures are the exception, because its
# specs assert on the file directly.
.pagination-changes.json
